    <profile name="The Watcher&apos;s Axe" id="b5b9-d979-68ee-f0b8" hidden="false" typeId="1d88-1369-f0ed-b39c" typeName="Melee Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Ability" typeId="2113-98a2-4376-a94c">The Watcher&apos;s Axe is a master-crafted power weapon that adds +3 to the wielder&apos;s strength. Additionally, any failed attempts To Wound made with it may be re-rolled.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Moment Shackle" id="4516-fcf9-c669-24be" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Once per battle, Trajann Valoris may break the Moment Shackle to perform one of the following feats:


- If Trajann would be removed from play after being reduced to 0 wounds, instead he is not removed and stands back up with D3 wounds remaining.
- After Trajann has fought during an assault this turn, he may fight a second time during the same assault at Initiative 0.
- Whenever Trajann or his unit is chosen as a target during the shooting or assault phase, Trajann gains a 2+ invulnerable save until the start of your next turn.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
  </sharedProfiles>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Only In Death" id="a226-a827-1018-b8bf" hidden="false">
      <description>Adeptus Custodes automatically pass tests to regroup, and may take such tests even if the squad has been reduced below half-strength, though all other criteria apply. Usually troops that regroup cannot move normally and always count as moving whether they do or not, but these restrictions do not apply to models with this special rule. If Adeptus Custodes are caught by a sweeping advance, they are not destroyed and will instead continue to fight normally. If this happens then the unit is subject to the No Retreat! rule in this round of close combat and might therefore suffer additional casualties.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
